{
  "uid": "stride-logs",
  "title": "Stride — Logs & traces",
  "description": "Backend logs from Loki with a click-through to the trace in Jaeger, the log-based alerts' signals, and the trace pipeline (OpenTelemetry Collector) health.",
  "editable": false,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "tags": ["stride", "logs", "traces"],
  "time": { "from": "now-1h", "to": "now" },
  "timepicker": {},
  "timezone": "browser",
  "version": 1,
  "links": [
    {
      "title": "Jaeger: backend traces (service 'strava')",
      "type": "link",
      "url": "http://localhost:16686/search?service=strava",
      "targetBlank": true
    },
    {
      "title": "Runbook: log alerts",
      "type": "link",
      "url": "https://github.com/erykszczesniak/Stride/blob/main/docs/runbooks/log-alerts.md",
      "targetBlank": true
    },
    {
      "title": "docs/observability.md",
      "type": "link",
      "url": "https://github.com/erykszczesniak/Stride/blob/main/docs/observability.md",
      "targetBlank": true
    }
  ],
  "annotations": { "list": [] },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "loki_datasource",
        "label": "Loki data source",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "loki",
        "current": { "selected": false, "text": "Loki", "value": "Loki" },
        "hide": 0,
        "refresh": 1
      },
      {
        "name": "prometheus_datasource",
        "label": "Prometheus data source",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus",
        "current": { "selected": false, "text": "Prometheus", "value": "Prometheus" },
        "hide": 0,
        "refresh": 1
      },
      {
        "name": "app",
        "label": "App",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "${loki_datasource}" },
        "definition": "label_values(app)",
        "query": { "label": "app", "refId": "LokiVariableQueryEditor-VariableQuery", "stream": "", "type": 1 },
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true,
        "allValue": ".+",
        "refresh": 2,
        "sort": 1,
        "current": { "selected": true, "text": ["strava-backend"], "value": ["strava-backend"] }
      },
      {
        "name": "level",
        "label": "Level",
        "type": "custom",
        "query": "ERROR,WARN,INFO,DEBUG",
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true,
        "allValue": ".+",
        "options": [
          { "selected": true, "text": "All", "value": "$__all" },
          { "selected": false, "text": "ERROR", "value": "ERROR" },
          { "selected": false, "text": "WARN", "value": "WARN" },
          { "selected": false, "text": "INFO", "value": "INFO" },
          { "selected": false, "text": "DEBUG", "value": "DEBUG" }
        ],
        "current": { "selected": true, "text": ["All"], "value": ["$__all"] }
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 0 },
      "id": 100,
      "title": "Logs — what the log-based alerts see (Loki)",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "ERROR lines per second, by app",
      "description": "rate of level=ERROR lines. LogErrorVolumeAboveBaseline fires when the last 10 minutes exceed 3x the previous hour's average; the Prometheus ErrorLogSpike reads the same signal from logback_events_total.",
      "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "${loki_datasource}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 1 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "lineWidth": 1, "fillOpacity": 15, "showPoints": "never" }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "${loki_datasource}" },
          "expr": "sum by (app) (rate({app=~\"$app\", level=\"ERROR\"}[$__auto]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{app}}",
          "queryType": "range"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Log volume by level",
      "description": "Lines per interval per level for the selected apps. A level that disappears is as interesting as one that spikes: no lines at all for 10 minutes is LogPipelineSilent.",
      "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "${loki_datasource}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 1 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "bars", "lineWidth": 1, "fillOpacity": 60, "stacking": { "mode": "normal", "group": "A" } }
        },
        "overrides": [
          { "matcher": { "id": "byName", "options": "ERROR" }, "properties": [{ "id": "color", "value": { "mode": "fixed", "fixedColor": "red" } }] },
          { "matcher": { "id": "byName", "options": "WARN" }, "properties": [{ "id": "color", "value": { "mode": "fixed", "fixedColor": "orange" } }] },
          { "matcher": { "id": "byName", "options": "INFO" }, "properties": [{ "id": "color", "value": { "mode": "fixed", "fixedColor": "green" } }] },
          { "matcher": { "id": "byName", "options": "DEBUG" }, "properties": [{ "id": "color", "value": { "mode": "fixed", "fixedColor": "blue" } }] }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "${loki_datasource}" },
          "expr": "sum by (level) (count_over_time({app=~\"$app\", level=~\".+\"}[$__auto]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{level}}",
          "queryType": "range"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "bargauge",
      "title": "Top loggers by ERROR lines (selected range)",
      "description": "Which class is writing the errors. LogExceptionRateSpikePerLogger fires per logger above 30 lines in 5 minutes; LoggingAspect is excluded there because it re-logs every controller exception, expected 404s included.",
      "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "${loki_datasource}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 9 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "color": { "mode": "continuous-RdYlGr" }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "displayMode": "gradient",
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false },
        "showUnfilled": true,
        "valueMode": "color"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "${loki_datasource}" },
          "expr": "topk(10, sum by (logger) (count_over_time({app=~\"$app\", level=\"ERROR\"} | logger != \"\" [$__auto])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{logger}}",
          "queryType": "instant",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Failed password logins (selected range)",
      "description": "'Bad credentials' errors from AuthenticationController.login(). LogAuthFailureSpike fires above 20 in 5 minutes: credential stuffing, or a client shipped with a broken login flow.",
      "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "${loki_datasource}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 6, "x": 12, "y": 9 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "color": { "mode": "thresholds" },
          "thresholds": { "mode": "absolute", "steps": [{ "color": "green", "value": null }, { "color": "orange", "value": 10 }, { "color": "red", "value": 20 }] }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false },
        "textMode": "value"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "${loki_datasource}" },
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({app=~\"$app\", level=\"ERROR\"} |= \"AuthenticationController.login() threw exception: Bad credentials\" [$__auto]))",
          "legendFormat": "failed logins",
          "queryType": "instant",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Lines with a traceId (selected range)",
      "description": "How many backend lines carry a trace id and can be followed into Jaeger. Lines written outside a request (startup, schedulers) have none.",
      "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "${loki_datasource}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 6, "x": 18, "y": 9 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "color": { "mode": "fixed", "fixedColor": "blue" }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false },
        "textMode": "value"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "${loki_datasource}" },
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({app=~\"$app\"} | traceId != \"\" [$__auto]))",
          "legendFormat": "lines with traceId",
          "queryType": "instant",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "logs",
      "title": "Backend logs — expand a line, click 'Trace in Jaeger' next to traceId",
      "description": "Live tail of the selected apps and levels. Every backend line carries traceId/spanId/logger as structured metadata; the Loki datasource's derived field turns traceId into a link to the trace in Jaeger, and Jaeger's 'Logs for this span' comes back here.",
      "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "${loki_datasource}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 14, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 17 },
      "options": {
        "dedupStrategy": "none",
        "enableLogDetails": true,
        "prettifyLogMessage": false,
        "showCommonLabels": false,
        "showLabels": false,
        "showTime": true,
        "sortOrder": "Descending",
        "wrapLogMessage": true
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "loki", "uid": "${loki_datasource}" },
          "expr": "{app=~\"$app\", level=~\"$level\"} | json | line_format \"{{.level}} {{.logger_name}} — {{.message}}\"",
          "queryType": "range"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 31 },
      "id": 200,
      "title": "Traces — the collector between the backend and Jaeger (Prometheus)",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Spans per second: received from the backend vs sent to Jaeger",
      "description": "The gap is tail sampling: every error-status or 4xx/5xx trace and every trace slower than 1 s is kept, the rest is sampled at 10 % (monitoring/otel/otel-collector.yml). Received at zero while the backend serves traffic means the backend is not reaching the collector.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${prometheus_datasource}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 32 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "lineWidth": 1, "fillOpacity": 10, "showPoints": "never" }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${prometheus_datasource}" },
          "expr": "sum(rate(otelcol_receiver_accepted_spans{app=\"otel-collector\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "received"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${prometheus_datasource}" },
          "expr": "sum(rate(otelcol_exporter_sent_spans{app=\"otel-collector\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "sent to Jaeger"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${prometheus_datasource}" },
          "expr": "sum(rate(otelcol_receiver_refused_spans{app=\"otel-collector\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "refused (memory limiter)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Tail sampling decisions per second, by policy",
      "description": "Traces kept by each policy (keep-errors = ERROR span status, keep-http-errors = 4xx/5xx outcome, keep-slow = over 1 s, baseline-10-percent) and traces dropped. A rising 'keep-errors' line is an incident signal in itself.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${prometheus_datasource}" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 32 },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0,
          "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "lineWidth": 1, "fillOpacity": 10, "showPoints": "never" }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom", "showLegend": true },
        "tooltip": { "mode": "multi", "sort": "desc" }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "${prometheus_datasource}" },
          "expr": "sum by (policy, sampled) (rate(otelcol_processor_tail_sampling_count_traces_sampled{app=\"otel-collector\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{policy}} sampled={{sampled}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "From an alert to the trace to the logs",
      "description": "The three clicks a responder makes; the long version is in docs/observability.md.",
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 40 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "1. **Alert → dashboard.** Every log-based alert (`LogAuthFailureSpike`, `LogExceptionRateSpikePerLogger`, `LogErrorVolumeAboveBaseline`, `LogPipelineSilent`) links here via `dashboard_url`; set *Level* to `ERROR` and, for the per-logger alert, add `| logger=\"<logger from the alert>\"` to the logs panel.\n2. **Log line → trace.** Expand a line in the logs panel: `traceId` shows a **Trace in Jaeger** button (Loki derived field → Jaeger datasource). The trace shows the request span and its async children, after PII redaction and tail sampling in the collector — errors and slow traces are always kept.\n3. **Trace → logs.** In the trace view, a span's **Logs for this span** runs `{app=\"strava-backend\"} |= \"<traceId>\"` in Loki, ±5 minutes around the span, so lines from async listeners are included.\n\nPipeline: backend (JSON, `traceId`/`spanId` in MDC) → Alloy (Docker discovery, labels `app`+`level`, structured metadata `logger`/`traceId`/`spanId`) → Loki (3 days, ruler → Alertmanager). Traces: backend → OpenTelemetry Collector (redaction, tail sampling) → Jaeger."
      }
    }
  ]
}
